      "archaeologicalRemains": "notvisible",
      "details": "<p>The imagery location of Ehursagtilla is based on\u00a0<a href=\"https://uppsala.app.box.com/s/cgm386mr39f0we39y8v49ktecc664k0k/file/722112939158\"><span>Peders\u00e9n 2021 fig. 2.2</span></a>, which shows a plan of eastern Babylon, with 200 m UTM coordinates given.\u00a0 The site of the temple of the god Ninurta is known since it was excavated in 1901. The remains of the building are no longer visible; they are just below the surface. The ruins of this 1780 m\u00b2 temple are located approximately at 32.530635, 44.426566.</p>",
